  "decision_summary": "Most direct absolute human oral bioavailability records for transferred molecules are below 20%, and qualitative reports consistently describe low or poor oral bioavailability. One fed-state danazol record exceeds 20%, but fasted danazol records are below 20%, so the overall weight supports low F.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Danazol's absolute bioavailability is strongly food-dependent (fasted 11-19%, fed 44-67%), making its threshold classification condition-dependent.",
    "Several records are qualitative ('low', 'poor') or unspecified bioavailability type rather than numeric absolute F values."
  ],
